betterquesting.quest.pbLvv9tvQaKGp2Y2usPMSw.name=§5§l§nUEV 유리
betterquesting.quest.pbLvv9tvQaKGp2Y2usPMSw.desc=붕규산 유리의 다음 단계는 인피니티입니다.

# Quest: A Not So Useful Scanner...
betterquesting.quest.pd68ySXjTD6yW1MN6x6swg.name=§6§l그다지 유용하지 않은 스캐너...
betterquesting.quest.pd68ySXjTD6yW1MN6x6swg.desc=...하지만 매우 유용한 측정기입니다.%n%nGT EU 측정기는 케이블과 기계의 전기에 대한 기본 정보를 제공합니다.%n%n[note]MV 단계에서 더 발전된 버전을 사용할 수 있으며, 훨씬 더 많은 데이터를 수집할 수 있으니 나중에 이 탭으로 돌아와서 찾아보십시오.[/note]

# Quest: Drones are not Drones!
betterquesting.quest.prKPwVNgSgOE1NGPiEEF-g.name=§6§l드론은 드론이 아닙니다!
betterquesting.quest.prKPwVNgSgOE1NGPiEEF-g.desc=...하지만 그들은 벌들만큼 부지런할 수 있습니다. 이 새로운 전기 동료들은 멀티블록 기계를 위한 완벽한 파트너입니다: 유지보수, 제어, 관리—모든 것을 처리할 수 있습니다.
%n
%n§6§lMaintenance§r
%nThe §5§lDrone Centre§r is a newly developed machine. It requires no power—simply place a drone into the input bus, and it will begin operation.
%n
%nReplacing the maintenance hatch on your Multiblock machines with a §lDrone Downlink Module§r will connect them to the drone network.
%n
%nOnce activated, the Drone Centre will automatically scan for all Downlink Modules within range and attempt to establish a connection with them. As long as the Drone Centre remains active, all connected Multiblock machines will [bold]never[/bold] suffer from annoying maintenance issues again!
%n
%n[note]Goodbye, my precious 256x superconductor base ingots that were lost due to maintenance failures...[/note]
%n
%n
%n§6§lEntity Drones§r
%nDrones now exist as physical entities, unlocking several new features:
%n
%n- When a maintenance issue occurs, a drone will deploy from the Downlink Module and perform a circular inspection flight around the affected machine.
%n- We've equipped drones with cameras! Click the §9§lObserve§r button in the GUI to access a real-time video feed from the drone. As long as you are in the same dimension, you can connect to the drone regardless of distance.
%n- While in observation mode, the WAILA HUD provides more information than normal. Additionally, aim your crosshair at a machine and press §2§lG§r to remotely open its GUI! This currently supports all GT machines and hatches. However, since drones are not equipped with robotic arms, item and fluid slots cannot be interacted with.
%n
%n
%n§6§lGroup Control & Statistics§r
%nThe Drone Centre provides a powerful machine management interface, supporting grouping, remote observation, batch power control, and machine renaming:
%n
%n- Connected machines can be organized into up to §664§r custom groups. Groups can be renamed, and a machine may belong to multiple groups.
%n- After selecting a group, power control actions will be applied to all machines within that group. Specifically, §6§lShift-clicking§r the shutdown button will set all machine controller covers to "Disable" mode.
%n- By enabling the built-in §5§lProduction Recorder§r, the Drone Centre can collect real-time statistics from all connected machines, including EU consumption, item throughput, and fluid throughput. All recorded data is stored directly inside the Drone Centre.
%n
%n
%n§6§lTiered Drones§r
%n[warn]Drones may crash during operation. The crash probability decreases from Tier 1 to Tier 3, and Tier 3 and Tier 4 Drones will never crash.[/warn]
%n
%nDon't worry—if a backup drone is available in the input bus, the Drone Centre will consume it instantly.
%n
%nUsing higher-tier drones increases the operating range of the Drone Centre:
%n
%n  §6•§r §l§3Drone (T1)§r
%n    - Range: §6128 blocks§r
%n    - Crash Chance: §61/28,800 per second§r (Average ~8 hours)
%n
%n  §6•§r §l§3Drone (T2)§r
%n    - Range: §6512 blocks§r
%n    - Crash Chance: §61/172,800 per second§r (Average ~48 hours)
%n
%n  §6•§r §l§3Drone (T3)§r
%n    - Range: §64,096 blocks§r
%n    - Crash Chance: §2Never§r
%n
%n  §6•§r §l§3Drone (T4)§r
%n    - Range: §64,096 blocks (Automatic) / Infinite (Matching Key)§r
%n    - Crash Chance: §2Never§r
%n    - Cross-dimension: §2Yes§r
%n
%n
%nTo enable cross-dimensional connections with a T4 Drone, configure matching keys on both the Drone Centre and the Downlink Module.
%n
%nThe Downlink Module can copy matching keys using a §lData Stick§r.
%n
